unilateral SpaceX decision or directed by U.S. officials. The heat shield from an engineering

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:59.167
standpoint comes into play after a deorbit burn, a retrograde firing that drops the low point

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:04.407
of the orbit into the atmosphere, and the capsule then faces that shield forward so one surface

00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:09.927
absorbs the kinetic energy of orbital velocity, peak heating hits at roughly 8 kilometers per

00:04:09.927 --> 00:04:14.887
second relative speed, and at 8 kilometers per second, each kilogram of vehicle carries

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:20.727
a back-of-envelope 32 million joules of kinetic energy, half times 8,000 meters per second

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.167
squared.

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:27.047
8 kilometers per second over a speed of sound near 340 meters per second is on the order

00:04:27.047 --> 00:04:32.667
of Mach 24, so the air ahead cannot move aside and compresses into a radiating plasma.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:38.867
The Pika X tiles, a carbon phenolic that charrs and throws heat out as radiation, radiate

00:04:38.867 --> 00:04:42.907
away the majority of that energy while the structure underneath stays below critical

00:04:42.907 --> 00:04:43.527
temperatures.

00:04:44.147 --> 00:04:49.007
Because those same tiles already flew on prior missions, the margins have to cover initial

00:04:49.007 --> 00:04:54.727
ablation, the sacrificial char wearing away, and any microcracking from repeated heat cycles.

00:04:55.287 --> 00:05:00.387
After peak heating, the vehicle deploys parachutes at subsonic speeds, shifting from plasma

00:05:00.387 --> 00:05:06.527
to timing, a drogue, the small first shoot, then the mains, so splash down loads stay inside

00:05:06.527 --> 00:05:07.567
the certified envelope.

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:13.387
What is inside stays protected because the pressure vessel, the sealed cabin, and the avionics

00:05:13.387 --> 00:05:18.787
bays, the flight computers and electronics sit behind multiple layers of insulation, plus

00:05:18.787 --> 00:05:22.427
active cooling loops that keep running until just before the shoots deploy.

00:05:23.107 --> 00:05:27.667
Over successive flights, the one piece swapped at scale is the heat shield coating, while

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:30.907
the main structure avionics and propulsion keep adding flights.

00:05:31.427 --> 00:05:36.227
So the extra cost of each cargo return is inspection, refurbishment labor, and a new

00:05:36.227 --> 00:05:38.567
set of parachutes rather than a whole new capsule.

00:05:39.307 --> 00:05:44.127
Wave a magic wand and you pay for coding, shoots, and technician time, not a new pressure

00:05:44.127 --> 00:05:44.487
vessel.

00:05:44.947 --> 00:05:50.267
